Package: bibliolab
Type: Package
Title: Guided Bibliometric Analysis and Text Mining
Version: 5.0.7
Date: 2026-10-21
Authors@R: 
    person("Manuel J.", "Sánchez-Franco", , "majesus@us.es", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8042-3550"))
Description: A guided 'shiny' application, together with a set of functions,
    to describe a bibliographic corpus (production, sources, authors,
    citations, references) and to explore its text with exploratory models:
    latent Dirichlet allocation, correspondence analysis, principal component
    analysis, UMAP with HDBSCAN, Jensen-Shannon divergence and co-occurrence
    networks. Decisions that change the results (number of topics, stability
    of clusters, sampling noise of divergences, chance baselines for axes)
    are assisted and recorded, and the analysis can be exported as a
    reproducible bundle with a methodological report, parameters, seeds and a
    replication script. It is designed for researchers without technical
    training, and all computation is local. Methodological references include
    Blei, Ng and Jordan (2003) <https://jmlr.org/papers/v3/blei03a.html> for
    latent Dirichlet allocation; McInnes, Healy and Melville (2018)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1802.03426> for UMAP; Campello, Moulavi and Sander
    (2013) <doi:10.1007/978-3-642-37456-2_14> for HDBSCAN; and Lin (1991)
    <doi:10.1109/18.61115> for Jensen-Shannon divergence.
